WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.770
It was a lovely summer day in the country.

2
00:00:03.771 --> 00:00:07.227
Mother Duck sat on her eggs for a long time.

3
00:00:07.228 --> 00:00:14.081
After a while, one by one, ducklings came out of the eggs.

4
00:00:14.082 --> 00:00:17.201
"Peep, peep! Peep, peep!"

5
00:00:17.202 --> 00:00:21.058
"Quack, quack! Are you all out?"

6
00:00:21.059 --> 00:00:28.027
"No, one egg is still here. Look how big it is!"

7
00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:35.122
At last the big egg hatched. This duckling was very big and very ugly.

8
00:00:35.123 --> 00:00:40.627
"Oh my! This duckling is big and different from the others.

9
00:00:40.628 --> 00:00:46.071
I wonder if it is a turkey. We will soon find out."

10
00:00:46.072 --> 00:00:49.097
Mother Duck took her ducklings to the water.

11
00:00:49.098 --> 00:00:53.930
One after another the little ducklings jumped into the water.

12
00:00:53.931 --> 00:00:59.966
The ugly duckling also jumped into the water and swam very well.

13
00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:06.018
"Oh, he is not a turkey. Turkeys can't swim. He is a duckling.

14
00:01:06.019 --> 00:01:13.715
Let's go to the farmyard. But you must stay close to me and watch out for the cat."

15
00:01:13.716 --> 00:01:18.117
"Look at that duckling! He looks so strange."

16
00:01:18.118 --> 00:01:21.606
"He is so big and ugly. Go away!"

17
00:01:21.607 --> 00:01:27.374
"Please, leave him alone. He is not doing any harm."

18
00:01:27.375 --> 00:01:30.475
But the ducks pecked the ugly duckling.

19
00:01:30.476 --> 00:01:36.282
All the animals in the farmyard bit him and pushed him too.

20
00:01:36.283 --> 00:01:39.622
"I wish the cat would eat you!"

21
00:01:39.623 --> 00:01:45.049
"You should never have been born."

22
00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:52.560
So the poor little duckling was very sad. Finally he ran away.

23
00:01:52.561 --> 00:02:00.794
"Why does everyone hate me? Is it because I am so ugly? But I am really nice."

24
00:02:00.795 --> 00:02:04.607
The ugly duckling met two wild ducks.

25
00:02:04.608 --> 00:02:06.671
"What kind of duck are you?"

26
00:02:06.672 --> 00:02:13.119
"You are really ugly. But that's okay if you don't marry a duck from our family."

27
00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:21.180
Then the ugly duckling heard pop, pop ! And the two wild ducks fell

28
00:02:21.181 --> 00:02:27.397
dead. Just then many hunting dogs appeared. The ugly duckling was very

29
00:02:27.398 --> 00:02:30.289
afraid. So he tucked his head under his

30
00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:36.712
wing. A hunting dog sniffed the ugly duckling. "Sniff, sniff! You are

31
00:02:36.713 --> 00:02:41.295
ugly!" And they went away without touching the ugly

32
00:02:41.296 --> 00:02:49.143
duckling. "Oh, I am alive! No one wants me. Even a dog doesn't want to bite

33
00:02:49.144 --> 00:02:53.675
me." He felt lucky, but at the same time he felt

34
00:02:53.676 --> 00:03:00.161
sad. The poor duckling waited for several hours and then ran

35
00:03:00.162 --> 00:03:05.046
away. A storm began. The rain and lightning terrified the ugly

36
00:03:05.047 --> 00:03:13.024
duckling. He was so cold and wet! He ran and ran as he looked for shelter from the

37
00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:22.065
storm. Finally he arrived at a cottage. An old woman, a cat, and a hen lived in this cottage. He went

38
00:03:22.066 --> 00:03:24.205
inside. "May I have some

39
00:03:24.206 --> 00:03:31.882
food?" "Oh, what a prize! Is it a fat duck? Now I can have duck

40
00:03:31.883 --> 00:03:34.619
eggs." The old woman's sight was very

41
00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.254
bad. So the duckling lived there for a few

42
00:03:38.255 --> 00:03:41.607
days. But the hen and the cat were mean to the duckling.

43
00:03:41.608 --> 00:03:44.302
"I can lay eggs. Can you do that?"

44
00:03:44.303 --> 00:03:46.318
"No."

45
00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:49.630
"I can catch a mouse. Can you do that?"

46
00:03:49.631 --> 00:03:51.298
"No."

47
00:03:51.299 --> 00:03:53.876
"Then what can you do?"

48
00:03:53.877 --> 00:03:56.026
"I can swim."

49
00:03:56.027 --> 00:04:00.683
"Oh, no one should swim! You will surely drown!"

50
00:04:00.684 --> 00:04:02.372
"I won't drown."

51
00:04:02.373 --> 00:04:05.166
"You are a big liar!"

52
00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:09.499
So the poor duckling left the cottage.

53
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:15.035
Soon summer turned into fall. The ugly duckling swam in the pond.

54
00:04:15.036 --> 00:04:19.388
A group of swans flew over the duckling.

55
00:04:19.389 --> 00:04:25.199
"What beautiful birds! I wish I could be like them."

56
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:30.654
The weather grew colder and colder. Then winter came.

57
00:04:30.655 --> 00:04:36.423
"I must swim and swim, or the pond will freeze around me."

58
00:04:36.424 --> 00:04:40.119
But every night the ice grew thicker and thicker.

59
00:04:40.132 --> 00:04:47.284
Finally the pond froze over, and the duckling couldn't move anymore.

60
00:04:47.285 --> 00:04:51.853
Early in the morning, a farmer saw the frozen duckling.

61
00:04:51.854 --> 00:04:58.423
"Oh, poor duckling! I'll take you home to my wife and children."

62
00:04:58.424 --> 00:05:04.392
The wife took care of the duckling. Soon the duckling got well.

63
00:05:04.393 --> 00:05:07.908
But the children wanted to play with the duckling.

64
00:05:07.909 --> 00:05:14.789
"Come and play with us! Come and play with us!" The duckling was scared.

65
00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:26.804
The farmer's wife and the children chased the duckling around the farm house. Finally he ran out the door.

66
00:05:26.805 --> 00:05:36.159
Spring came and everything was beautiful. The ugly duckling saw the butterflies dancing and heard the birds singing.

67
00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:39.667
One day his wings felt very strong.

68
00:05:39.668 --> 00:05:46.249
So he flapped them against his sides and flew high into the sky.

69
00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:51.650
"Wow, I can fly so high! What's happened to me?"

70
00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:55.104
The ugly duckling saw a beautiful garden with a pond.

71
00:05:55.105 --> 00:06:00.632
He decided to rest there for a while.

72
00:06:00.633 --> 00:06:08.154
Just then three swans swam out of the bushes by the pond. He remembered the beautiful birds.

73
00:06:08.155 --> 00:06:11.557
"I want to stay with these beautiful birds.

74
00:06:11.558 --> 00:06:15.855
But they will kill me because I am so ugly.

75
00:06:15.856 --> 00:06:21.366
At least I will die happily if I can be with them for a while."

76
00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:29.004
So he swam towards the swans. When the swans saw the young bird, they swam to him.

77
00:06:29.005 --> 00:06:34.735
"Peck me if you must!" And he bent his head down to the surface of the water.

78
00:06:34.736 --> 00:06:40.683
But the ugly duckling saw a beautiful swan looking back at him in the water!

79
00:06:40.684 --> 00:06:46.732
"Oh! Is that really me? I am a beautiful swan!

80
00:06:46.733 --> 00:06:50.033
I am not an ugly duckling after all!"

81
00:06:50.034 --> 00:06:55.353
The three swans welcomed the young swan.

82
00:06:55.354 --> 00:07:00.883
Some children came to the pond and threw pieces of bread into the water.

83
00:07:00.884 --> 00:07:09.439
"Look, there is another swan! This new one is the most beautiful of all."

84
00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:15.478
The ugly duckling was so happy. He was more beautiful than he had ever hoped to be.

85
00:07:15.479 --> 00:07:23.301
And now he knew where he belonged.

